{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"relay-module","name":"Relay module","version":"1.0.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"A 5 V relay on a module: a board's pin switches a separate circuit (a lamp, a motor, a pump) through its COM, NO and NC contacts. It clicks.","category":"Power","needsApp":"0.3.0","code":"// A relay module: IN drives a transistor that powers the relay's coil; the coil pulls the switch\n// over (COM to NO) and a spring pulls it back (COM to NC). The two sides share no wires.\nbench.device('relay', (part) => {\n  const led = part.screen('led');\n  const snd = part.sound();\n  const activeLow = part.params.trigger !== 'high';\n  let on = false, powered = false, clickUntil = -1, clicks = 0;\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      const vcc = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\n      powered = vcc >= 3.8;\n      if (powered) io.drive('IN', vcc, 0); // (its pull-up resistor: weaker than any pin)\n      else io.release('IN');\n      const lvl = io.level('IN');\n      // IN has a pull-up on the module: unwired means HIGH\n      const asked = powered && (activeLow ? lvl === 0 : lvl === 1);\n      if (asked !== on) {\n        on = asked;\n        clicks++;\n        clickUntil = io.time + 0.012;\n      }\n      io.connect('COM', 'NO', on);\n      io.connect('COM', 'NC', !on);\n      if (io.time < clickUntil) snd.tone(on ? 140 : 110, 0.5, 'square');\n      else snd.stop();\n      led.set(0, 0, on ? 1 : 0);\n      io.draw(on ? 0.07 : powered ? 0.002 : 0);\n    },\n    status() {\n      if (!powered) return ['no power (VCC needs 5 V): stays off, COM joined to NC'];\n      return [on ? 'on: COM joined to NO' : 'off: COM joined to NC', `${clicks} clicks`];\n    },\n  };\n});\n","parts":[{"id":"relay1","name":"Relay module (1 channel)","description":"Control side: VCC (5 V), GND, IN. Most modules switch on when IN is LOW (pick in its settings). Load side: COM is joined to NO (normally open) while it's on, and to NC (normally closed) while it's off. The coil takes about 70 mA: more than a pin can give, which is why it's a module (with its own transistor).","swatch":"#2f5fb8","mass":15,"sound":true,"params":[{"key":"trigger","label":"Switches on when IN is","kind":"select","options":[{"value":"low","label":"LOW (most modules)"},{"value":"high","label":"HIGH"}]}],"defaults":{"trigger":"low"},"shape":[{"box":[5,0.16,2.6],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#1d4fb8"},{"box":[1.9,1.5,1.5],"at":[0.4,0.91,0],"color":"#2f5fb8"},{"box":[1,0.8,1.6],"at":[2,0.56,0],"color":"#3d8ae8"},{"screen":{"id":"led","size":[0.3,0.3],"px":[1,1],"mode":"pixels","on":"#ff3020","off":"#3a1210","bg":"#1d4fb8"},"at":[-1.6,0.17,0.8]}],"pins":[{"id":"VCC","label":"VCC (5 V)","at":[-2.3,0.16,0.254],"kind":"vin","vmin":4,"vmax":5.5},{"id":"GND","at":[-2.3,0.16,0],"kind":"gnd"},{"id":"IN","at":[-2.3,0.16,-0.254],"kind":"in","pulled":"up"},{"id":"NO","label":"NO (normally open)","at":[2.4,0.95,0.5],"kind":"motor"},{"id":"COM","label":"COM","at":[2.4,0.95,0],"kind":"motor"},{"id":"NC","label":"NC (normally closed)","at":[2.4,0.95,-0.5],"kind":"motor"}],"device":"relay"}],"examples":[{"name":"Relay blinks a lamp","description":"A board switches a relay once a second; the relay switches an LED that has its own 9 V battery. Two circuits, one shared nothing: that's what a relay is for.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Relay blinks a lamp","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-8,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"relay","type":"relay-module/relay1","name":"Relay","params":{"trigger":"low"},"parent":null,"pos":[2,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"bat","type":"battery-9v","name":"Lamp battery (9 V)","params":{"charge":100},"parent":null,"pos":[10,0,6],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"lamp","type":"led","name":"Lamp","params":{"color":"yellow"},"parent":null,"pos":[10,0,-4],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP15"},"b":{"uid":"relay","pin":"IN"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"5V"},"b":{"uid":"relay","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"relay","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"bat","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"relay","pin":"COM"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"relay","pin":"NO"},"b":{"uid":"lamp","pin":"A"},"color":"#f08c2a"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"lamp","pin":"K"},"b":{"uid":"bat","pin":"-"},"color":"#2b2d33"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// A relay switching a lamp on its own battery. This relay module turns on when IN is LOW.\n#define RELAY 15\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  pinMode(RELAY, OUTPUT);\n  digitalWrite(RELAY, HIGH);   // off to start with\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  Serial.println(\"lamp on\");\n  digitalWrite(RELAY, LOW);    // on (click)\n  delay(1000);\n  Serial.println(\"lamp off\");\n  digitalWrite(RELAY, HIGH);   // off (click)\n  delay(1000);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}}]}